# evidence-for: AC-013, FR-009, FR-010, CT-001, ST-004, NFR-001
# evidence-timeout: 300
#
# GRIND cycle 12 -- D-088, D-089 and D-092, driven through server.py's real
# _DISPATCH table, which is the surface all three were found on.
#
# The three are ONE defect wearing three faces: the Foundry-Fix gate comparing
# STRINGS where it had to compare what the strings NAME. Each block prints the
# post-fix verdict and then the PRE-fix verdict, obtained by restoring that one
# comparison's old semantics in process -- the mutation is what makes the drive
# falsifiable, because a fix whose pins pass against the pre-fix code is not
# pinning anything.
#
#   D-088  `symbol` carries the durable `path#Symbol` cite form FR-004/AC-005
#          mandate and the four stream agent files instruct. The own-symbol
#          rule compared that whole string against a BARE leaf, so it could
#          never be equal and AC-013's distinctness rule was inert for the 26
#          of this run's 87 records (30%) that use that spelling. Honouring the
#          cite policy is what disabled the fix gate: the two requirements
#          actively fought, and the gate lost.
#   D-089  Wrong in both directions at once. A test INSIDE the defect's own
#          file cleared the own-file rule on the strength of its `::test_x`
#          suffix -- the defect closed with no adjacent path tested at all --
#          while `./adjacent/file.py::test_x`, a legitimate relative spelling
#          of a genuinely adjacent path, was refused as a dangling separator.
#          Normalisation therefore runs BEFORE the shape ladder, and block b
#          shows it did not become a bypass for the own file. Block c is the
#          statement half: `_statement_problem` caught a statement that IS the
#          path verbatim and never one naming it inside a sentence.
#   D-092  The statement and the reference were judged INDEPENDENTLY -- the
#          statement was not even a parameter of the reference check -- so a
#          test driving none of the paths the statement named closed the
#          defect. That is the whole of FR-010's word "NAMED": A-017 defines
#          the statement as naming the adjacent paths, so the two declarations
#          are a matched pair and the reference must drive one of them.
#
# Fixed as ONE normalisation layer with every comparison site bound to it, not
# as three patches. This run's repeated failure is never one bad rule -- it is
# one rule fixed in a single copy, which is D-038 -> D-050 -> D-076 -> D-085 ->
# D-088 -- so the last block states the invariant over the whole gate rather
# than per rule: however the defect's own location is spelled, the same three
# references get the same three verdicts.
#
# The two judgement calls, both resolved toward ACCEPTING, because refusing a
# real answer is this gate's characteristic failure and it fires in GRIND where
# the teammate has no way around it (that is what D-076 and D-085 both were):
# the statement's path rule is a SUBSET test over the whole declaration rather
# than a search, so an adjacent caller living in the defect's own file is still
# an answer; and the linkage rung accepts on ANY single shared token, is
# withheld when the statement failed its own ladder, and does not judge a
# reference that names a test FILE, because a container's name is not a claim
# about which path is driven. The lexical `same` pattern that produced D-085 is
# untouched -- verified from the compiled patterns in test_fix_gate.py's
# test_the_own_path_rule_landed_as_a_path_rule_not_a_widened_phrase.
== D-088: one defect, one reference, only the SHAPE of the symbol field differs ==
   post-fix  REFUSED  symbol=evict_stale
   post-fix  REFUSED  symbol=src/auth/sweeper.py#evict_stale
   post-fix  REFUSED  symbol=src/auth/sweeper.py:88#evict_stale
   PRE-fix   REFUSED  symbol=evict_stale
   PRE-fix   ACCEPTED symbol=src/auth/sweeper.py#evict_stale
   PRE-fix   ACCEPTED symbol=src/auth/sweeper.py:88#evict_stale
   a bare leaf never equals a path-qualified string, so AC-013 distinctness was dead for the cite form FR-004 mandates -- 26 of this run 87 records.

== D-089a: a test INSIDE the defect own file ==
   post-fix  REFUSED  src/auth/session.py::test_login_handler_refreshes
   PRE-fix   ACCEPTED src/auth/session.py::test_login_handler_refreshes
   whole-reference equality refused the bare file and let the ::suffix walk past, so the defect closed with no adjacent path tested.

== D-089b: a ./relative spelling, of an adjacent path and of the own file ==
   post-fix  ACCEPTED ./tests/test_sweeper.py::test_sweeper_evicts_stale
   post-fix  REFUSED  ./src/auth/session.py::test_login_handler_refreshes   (the OWN file)
   PRE-fix   REFUSED  ./tests/test_sweeper.py::test_sweeper_evicts_stale
   PRE-fix   REFUSED  ./src/auth/session.py::test_login_handler_refreshes   (the OWN file)
   the relative form was refused as a separator that delimits nothing, so the answer could not be written the way a teammate types it -- and normalising it does not become a bypass for the own file.

== D-089c: a statement whose ONLY named path is the defect own ==
   post-fix  REFUSED  names src/auth/session.py and nothing else
   post-fix  ACCEPTED names src/auth/session.py AND tools/audit.py
   PRE-fix   ACCEPTED names src/auth/session.py and nothing else
   PRE-fix   ACCEPTED names src/auth/session.py AND tools/audit.py
   a SUBSET test over the whole declaration, not a search: an adjacent caller may live in the defect own file, so naming it beside another path is still an answer. The lexical same pattern is untouched (D-085).

== D-092: does the referenced test drive a path the STATEMENT named? ==
   post-fix  REFUSED  tests/test_billing.py::test_invoice_totals_round_half_up
   post-fix  ACCEPTED tests/test_billing.py::test_login_handler_still_refreshes
   post-fix  ACCEPTED tests/test_billing.py                    (a test FILE -- not judged)
   post-fix  REFUSED  statement none -- linkage withheld, the statement is the problem
   PRE-fix   ACCEPTED tests/test_billing.py::test_invoice_totals_round_half_up
   PRE-fix   ACCEPTED tests/test_billing.py::test_login_handler_still_refreshes
   PRE-fix   ACCEPTED tests/test_billing.py                    (a test FILE -- not judged)
   PRE-fix   REFUSED  statement none -- linkage withheld, the statement is the problem
   same defect, same statement, same test FILE, same locator shape -- only the test NAME changes. ANY single shared token accepts: the rung is the weakest rule that closes D-092, because refusing a real answer in GRIND is what D-076 and D-085 both were.

